\nThis includes the following streams and drainages...\nFall Creek, Deep Creek, Big Bear Creek, Muddy Creek, Saltado Creek,\nSouth Fork San Miguel River, Dolores River, Specie Creek, San\nMiguel River, Leopard Creek and Alder Creek.","ends":"2026-09-15T17:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"San Miguel, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f00f6b1fbe35777ec9c1a4152399d983439fbca1.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f00f6b1fbe35777ec9c1a4152399d983439fbca1.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued September 15 at 12:00PM MDT until September 18 at 12:00AM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of southwest Colorado, including the following\nareas, Animas River Basin, Four Corners/Upper Dolores River,\nNorthwest San Juan Mountains, San Juan River Basin and Southwest\nSan Juan Mountains.\n\n* WHEN...From Wednesday afternoon through Thursday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nThis also includes the Gold Mountain, Elk and Ferris burn scars as\nwell as areas of steep, susceptible terrain.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Recent heavy rainfall in southwest Colorado has led to already\nsaturated ground. In addition, multiple rounds of showers and\nthunderstorms are expected Wednesday afternoon through Thursday\nevening producing periods of heavy rainfall and potential flash\nflooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-09-18T00:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3cf39aa90455238aaed4fdb23ced03f0914e3184.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3cf39aa90455238aaed4fdb23ced03f0914e3184.002.1"}],"afd":{